  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \nSurface high pressure centered over the southern Great Lakes early \nthis morning will shift off to the east through tonight. This will \nlead to continued cool temperatures today with afternoon highs only\nranging from the lower 50s north to the upper 50s in the south. \n\nLows tonight will range from the lower 30s in the far northeast to \nthe upper 30s in the southwest. Will go ahead and upgrade the Freeze \nWatch to a Freeze Warning for tonight across our far northeast. Some \npatchy frost will be possible elsewhere across our eastern areas but \nwith the potential for winds to pick up a bit later tonight, will \nlimit the mention of frost for now. \n\nWe will then start to get into return flow on the back side of the \nhigh with temperatures rebounding back into the 70s by Tuesday. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2) \nA weak mid level short wave will bring a chance for showers and few \nthunderstorms to the area on Wednesday. A somewhat stronger short \nwave will lead to a better chance for showers and thunderstorms \nFriday into Friday night.",
